---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/content/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../config/site';

const path = '/cookies/';
---
<BaseLayout
  title={`Cookie Notice for ${siteConfig.siteName} Analytics`}
  description={`How ${siteConfig.siteName} uses cookies for optional analytics with Consent Mode v2. Document generators work without cookies; details and choices explained.`}
  path={path}
>
  <Breadcrumbs items={[{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'Cookies', path }]} />
  <h1>Cookie notice</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    Our document generators do not require cookies to fill forms, preview documents, or export PDF/DOCX.
    Everything in the editor runs in your browser.
  </p>

  <h2>What we use cookies for</h2>
  <p>
    Cookies and similar storage fall into two buckets on this site: (1) optional analytics if you accept the cookie bar, and
    (2) advertising cookies only if Google AdSense is enabled in site configuration. Generators themselves rely on in-page
    JavaScript and optional <code>localStorage</code> drafts—not cookies—to work.
  </p>

  <h2>Analytics and Consent Mode</h2>
  <p>
    If Google Analytics (GA4) is configured, we load it only after you accept the cookie bar (or if you
    previously accepted). Until then, Google Consent Mode v2 defaults keep <code>analytics_storage</code>
    denied. The GA script is deferred until after page load / idle so it is not render-blocking.
  </p>
  <p>
    Choosing <strong>Accept</strong> stores <code>docuforge:cookie-ok=1</code> in localStorage and loads
    analytics (when configured). Choosing <strong>Reject</strong> stores
    <code>docuforge:cookie-ok=0</code> and keeps analytics off. Clearing site data shows the bar again.
    That localStorage key is an internal preference flag, not a third-party tracking cookie.
  </p>

  <h2>Advertising</h2>
  <p>
    Google AdSense is off unless explicitly enabled in site configuration. When ads are on, Google and partners may set
    advertising cookies as described in the
    <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>. For EEA/UK/CH traffic, a Google-certified CMP should be added before personalized
    ads are shown.
  </p>
  <p>
    You can limit personalized ads via
    <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Ad Settings</a>
    and industry opt-outs at
    <a href="https://optout.aboutads.info/" rel="noopener noreferrer">aboutads.info</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Local drafts (not cookies)</h2>
  <p>
    Optional “save draft” controls store form field values in <code>localStorage</code> on your device so you can leave a tool
    and return later. Those drafts are not sent to our servers. Clearing site data or using each tool’s clear-draft control
    removes them. Draft keys are separate from the cookie-consent preference described above.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <p>
    Use the on-site Accept / Reject controls, then browser settings to block or delete cookies if you change your mind.
    Rejecting analytics does not disable the document generators. For corrections or privacy questions, see
    <a href="/contact/">Contact</a> and the <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
